      "name": "JF Content With Icon Box",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "THE DISTINCTION OF BESPOKE ARTISTRY",
        "heading": "The Maker's Mark: What Is a True Custom Wedding Dress?",
        "intro": "<p>In a world of mass-produced bridal wear, a true custom wedding dress is a rarity. It starts with a blank page—a garment that does not exist until you and Julie Sufi vision it into being. Unlike Made-to-Order dresses, which are simply standard sizes adjusted to your height, a bespoke gown is built from the ground up. It begins not with a rack of samples, but with a hand-drawn illustration and a roll of raw fabric.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Rectangle_22924.png",
        "content": "<p>There is a profound difference between a bridal boutique and a working atelier. In a retail environment, you speak to a stylist; at Julie Sufi, you speak to the maker.</p><p>This is the <strong>Maker's Mark</strong>—the technical assurance that the person designing your gown is the same hand that understands the grain of the silk, the tension of the corsetry, and the physics of the drape.</p>",
        "button_label": "BOOK A FREE CONSULTATION",
        "button_link": "",
        "background_color": "#ffffff",
        "text_color": "#232128",
        "button_background_color": "#1f1f23",
        "button_text_color": "#ffffff",
        "padding_top_mobile": 44,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 44,
        "padding_top_desktop": 56,
        "padding_bottom_desktop": 64
      }
    },
